/; EXPECT_ERROR: Runtime Error: Cannot cast Dynamic value to Int32.
/; A null dynamic value carries the NIRAST tag, which is not a number, so the
/; same refusal applies as for a string or a bool. This used to return 0: the
/; null literal was written into the box as a raw pointer, which left the tag
/; reading as INT32 with a zero payload, so the cast "succeeded" on a value
/; that was never an int. Passing the same literal as an ARGUMENT put garbage
/; in the payload instead, and the cast returned that.
var _null = null
println(Int32(_null))
